    "i_en": "Read this ten minutes before the session. The most common failure is a student settling for 'upset' or 'fine' — push for the sharper word: frustrated, or afraid, or embarrassed? The precise name calms because it makes sense of the feeling. Never correct a feeling; a feeling isn't right or wrong, only the action after it is. This session sets up 'Pause, Then Choose'.",
